    <span class="marquee-kicker">Your choices</span>
    <h1 id="privacy-title">Privacy</h1>
    <p>Eat My Movies is run by James in the United Kingdom. For privacy questions or requests, email <a href="mailto:eatmymovies@hotmail.com">eatmymovies@hotmail.com</a>.</p>
    <h2>Information you give us</h2>
    <p>If you email us, we use your address and message to respond and manage your enquiry. Please avoid sending sensitive information. You can ask us to delete your message by emailing us.</p>
    <h2>Optional tracking</h2>
    <p>With your choice, we use Google Analytics to understand visits and Hotjar to understand how visitors interact with pages. These services may use cookies or similar browser storage and receive information about your device and activity on this site. We do not load either tool until you accept optional tracking. Your choice is saved in your browser's local storage so we can remember it. You can reject it or change your choice using “Tracking preferences” in the footer. Our basis for this optional tracking is your consent.</p>
    <p>See the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google privacy policy</a> and <a href="https://www.hotjar.com/legal/policies/privacy/" rel="noopener noreferrer">Hotjar privacy policy</a> for information about their processing, retention and international transfers.</p>
    <h2>Essential site functions and external content</h2>
    <p>The admin area uses an authentication cookie to keep its administrator signed in. It expires after eight hours, although activity can renew that period. Movie posters and details may be requested from TMDb, and following a streaming link takes you to an external site. Those providers may receive technical information, such as your IP address, when your browser connects to them.</p>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can contact us to ask about personal information we hold about you, request correction or deletion, or withdraw tracking consent. You can also raise a concern with the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" rel="noopener noreferrer">UK Information Commissioner’s Office</a>.</p>
</section>
